then enjoyed a snowball on the deck outside while watching the ships sail up the Mississippi. Having never been to a Mardi Gras parade, it was amazing to see the scale of the floats up close."},{"business_id":"BVOjxoXijWPfINv1eUGDKw","review_id":"YVQOc2AuigcVhl0tDFH0eA","date":"2018-03-27T19:25:08","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9502067565917969,"text_excerpt":"What a great tour! If you have time, recommend to check this place out. It was awesome to learn about Mardi Gras history, and to see the design process to make the floats."},{"business_id":"BVOjxoXijWPfINv1eUGDKw","review_id":"RtLqMdZcPBMFJ7cqBEssnA","date":"2019-08-28T19:26:22","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9479926228523254,"text_excerpt":"This was my \"must-do\" on our trip. I'm obsessed with Mardi Gras. This place is incredible! We got to learn how they made props and floats come to life from beginning to end. There's a cool video at the beginning that teaches you about the history behind Mardi Gras in New Orleans and you get some king cake (highlight!). Then you're led through the warehouse. You see models that have just been started, ones that are being repurposed, and ones that are complete. The amount of time and work that goes into it all is mind boggling! We had a blast here, perfect for those silly photos and great for kids."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
